IMPLEMENTATION DOCUMENT
Design Thinking World — Empathy & Define State
Phaser 3 Tile-Based Game


1. Project Overview
This document describes the full technical implementation of the Design Thinking World game's Empathy & Define State. The game is built using Phaser 3 with the Tiled map editor workflow described in Mike Westhad's Phaser 3 tilemap blog post series (post-1 pattern). The world is a bounded, top-down tile-based urbanized village with task houses, NPCs, and an upgradeable zone.

1.1 Tech Stack
Layer	Technology
Game Engine	Phaser 3 (v3.60+)
Map Editor	Tiled Map Editor (v1.10+)
Map Format	Tiled JSON export → loaded via Phaser loader
Tileset	16x16 or 32x32 pixel art tileset PNG
Language	JavaScript (ES6 modules)
UI Overlays	Phaser DOM / Game Objects for task panels
State Management	Plain JS object (GameState)

2. Phaser 3 Tilemap Setup (Post-1 Pattern)
Following the mikewesthad blog post-1 pattern, the map is loaded and rendered as follows:

2.1 Asset Loading (preload scene)
In the preload() function, load the tilemap JSON and tileset image:

  this.load.tilemapTiledJSON('map', 'assets/map/village.json');
  this.load.image('tiles', 'assets/tilesets/village-tiles.png');

2.2 Map Creation (create scene)
  const map = this.make.tilemap({ key: 'map' });
  const tileset = map.addTilesetImage('village-tiles', 'tiles');
  const groundLayer = map.createLayer('Ground', tileset, 0, 0);
  const wallLayer = map.createLayer('Walls', tileset, 0, 0);
  const objectLayer = map.createLayer('Objects', tileset, 0, 0);
  wallLayer.setCollisionByExclusion([-1]);

2.3 Tiled Layer Structure
Layer Name	Type	Purpose
Ground	Tile Layer	Grass, paths, plaza tiles
Walls	Tile Layer (collision)	Boundary walls, fences, buildings
Objects	Tile Layer	Trees, benches, decorations
Buildings	Tile Layer	Task houses, shop building
Upgrade	Tile Layer (dynamic)	Upgradeable tiles (flowers, lamps, etc.)
NPCs	Object Layer	NPC spawn points with properties
Spawn	Object Layer	Player spawn point

3. Map Design Specifications
3.1 Map Dimensions
    • Map size: 25 x 20 tiles
    • Tile size: 32 x 32 pixels
    • World pixel size: 800 x 640 pixels
    • Camera: follows player, clamped to world bounds

3.2 Task House Positions (tile coordinates)
House	Task	Tile X,Y	NPC Patrol
House 1	Define Problem Statement	4, 4	3–5, 6
House 2	Empathize & Story	20, 4	19–21, 6
House 3	Find a User + Draw	4, 12	3–5, 14
House 4	Sad/Happy Space	20, 12	19–21, 14
House 5	My Product Will Help	12, 4	11–13, 6
Shop	Upgrade Zone Shop	21, 16	20–22, 18

3.3 Player Spawn
    • Spawn position: tile 12, 18 (bottom-center)
    • Guide NPC stands at tile 12, 16 and walks one tile forward on game start

4. NPC System
4.1 NPC Types
NPC Type	Count	Behaviour
Guide NPC	1	Walks toward player at spawn, triggers welcome dialog, stays near entrance
Task NPCs	5	Patrol 2–3 tiles in front of assigned house. Show ! bubble. Trigger task panel on interact.
Shopkeeper NPC	1	Stands at shop door. Opens upgrade shop panel on interact.
Villager NPCs	3–4	Random idle walk on paths and benches. No interaction. Add world life.

4.2 NPC Interaction Flow
    1. Player walks near NPC (within 1 tile radius)
    2. NPC shows '!' speech bubble above head
    3. Player presses Spacebar or E to interact
    4. Phaser emits 'npc:interact' event with npcId
    5. UIManager opens corresponding task panel

5. Task Panel System
5.1 Panel Architecture
Each task panel is a Phaser DOM element (this.add.dom) overlaid on the game canvas. The game input is disabled while a panel is open. Panels are built as HTML/CSS components injected into the DOM.

5.2 Panel Components by Task
Task	Panel Name	Key UI Components
Task 1	ProblemStatement	Welcome message, single text field, submit button
Task 2	EmpathizeDefine	6-question form (Who, What, When, Where, How, Why)
Task 3a	FindAUser	6-question form + canvas draw area
Task 3b	SadHappySpace	Two canvas areas (sad + happy) with text/draw toggle
Task 4	MyProductWillHelp	Problem selection form inside fixed map boundary

5.3 Points Award on Completion
Task	Points Awarded	Trigger
Task 1 — Problem Statement	20 pts	On valid text submit
Task 2 — Empathize Story	30 pts	All 6 fields filled
Task 3a — Find a User	30 pts + 10 bonus	6 fields + drawing submitted
Task 3b — Sad/Happy Canvas	25 pts	Both canvases submitted
Task 4 — My Product Helps	35 pts	Problem selection submitted

6. Upgrade System
6.1 Upgrade Data Model
Each upgrade is a JS object stored in the GameState:

  { id: 'flowers', label: 'Plant Flowers', cost: 10, purchased: false,
    tileX: 18, tileY: 15, tileId: 42, layer: 'Upgrade' }

6.2 Upgrade Catalogue
Upgrade	Cost	Map Change
Plant Flowers	10 pts	Soil tiles → flower tiles in upgrade zone
Water Garden	15 pts	Dry grass tiles → lush green tiles
Add Park Bench	10 pts	Empty tile → bench tile + villager NPC spawns
Add a Pet	20 pts	Cat or dog sprite NPC appears near fountain
Upgrade Fountain	30 pts	Small fountain tile → large animated fountain
Add Street Lamps	15 pts	Dark path tiles → lamp tile with glow overlay
Paint a Mural	25 pts	Plain wall tile → painted mural tile

6.3 Tile Swap on Purchase
When a student buys an upgrade, putTileAt() is called on the Upgrade layer to swap the tile ID:

  upgradeLayer.putTileAt(newTileId, upgrade.tileX, upgrade.tileY);

7. HUD (Heads-Up Display)
    • Rendered as a fixed Phaser container (setScrollFactor(0)) at top of screen
    • Shows: star icon + point total | task progress bar (0/5 tasks)
    • Points counter animates (tween) when points are added
    • Task progress bar fills one segment per completed task

8. Scene Structure
Scene	Responsibility
BootScene	Load minimal assets, show loading bar
CharSelectScene	Male / female character selection UI
GameScene	Main world: map, player, NPCs, camera, HUD, upgrades
UIScene	Runs in parallel. Handles all task panels and shop UI
CompleteScene	Shown after all 5 tasks done. Celebrates completion.

9. File / Folder Structure
src/
  scenes/  BootScene.js | CharSelectScene.js | GameScene.js | UIScene.js
  objects/ Player.js | NPC.js | Villager.js
  ui/      TaskPanel.js | ShopPanel.js | HUD.js
  data/    upgrades.js | tasks.js | gameState.js
  utils/   EventBus.js | SaveManager.js
assets/
  map/     village.json (Tiled export)
  tilesets/village-tiles.png
  sprites/ player-male.png | player-female.png | npcs.png | pets.png